Landscape 844x390: sheet top is -46, meaning the header/title is clipped off-screen. The done button is visible at bottom, scroll area 226, first option visible. But the sheet title/close button are clipped above viewport, making close button inaccessible except backdrop/Escape? The backdrop click maybe works. But this is a usability bug for landscape. The original requirement is mobile; landscape is less critical, but user may rotate. We should fix `.sheet` for short landscape so header fits. Use max-height: 100dvh and overflow hidden? The sheet height is intrinsic 436 (390+46). We need reduce padding and content. At max-height 520 landscape media query, add shop-specific adjustments:
- `.sheet{ padding:6px 16px calc(10px + var(--safe-b)); border-radius:18px 18px 0 0; }`
- `.sheet-grip{ margin:0 auto 8px; }`
- `.sheet-head h2{ font-size:19px; }`
- `.eyebrow{ display:none; }`
- `.sheet-copy{ display:none; }` (or smaller)
- `.shop-scroll{ max-height: 52dvh; }` currently 58dvh=226
- `.shop-options{ grid-template-columns:repeat(6,1fr); }`? That would make tiny option cards; maybe not.
- `.sheet-btn{ height:40px; }`
- `.sheet-head{...}`

At 390 height, current scroll 226 at 58dvh. Total non-scroll overhead: 436-226=210. Need overhead <= 390 with some top margin, say <= 380. Reduce overhead by ~60. Removing eyebrow+copy (~58) and reducing paddings would fix.

The sheet is bottom-anchored and has `padding:10px 20px calc(20px + safe-b)` = 30 vertical + grip 20 + head 44? + copy ~40 + margins ~22 + button 50 + scroll 226 = 432. Remove copy (maybe keep one line?), hide eyebrow, reduce margins → ~380.

Let's add landscape-specific rules:
```
@media (orientation: landscape) and (max-height: 520px){
  .sheet{ padding:6px 16px calc(8px + var(--safe-b)); border-radius:18px 18px 0 0; }
  .sheet-grip{ margin:0 auto 8px; }
  .eyebrow{ display:none; }
  .sheet-copy{ margin:4px 0 6px; font-size:10.5px; line-height:1.35; }
  .shop-scroll{ max-height: 48dvh; margin-bottom:8px; }
  .shop-category{ margin-top:8px; }
  .shop-category-head{ margin-bottom:5px; }
  .shop-option{ min-height:78px; padding:5px 4px 4px; }
  .shop-options{ gap:6px; }
  .sheet-btn{ height:40px; }
  .sheet-head h2{ font-size:19px; }
  .sheet-close{ width:30px;height:30px;font-size:19px; }
}
```
Calculate overhead: padding 14, grip 12, head ~30, copy ~22, scroll 48dvh=187, margin 8, button 40 = 313? Total ~313, sheet top 77. Good.

At 320x568 portrait sheet top 23 fine. At 360x640 top 53. Fine.

But is this scope creep? It ensures shop usable in landscape. Good.

Note the existing landscape media query sets `.btn{height:44px}` globally, so `.sheet-btn` is a `.btn` too and gets 44; our 40 later in file? The landscape query is after the shop CSS and our new rules if placed within the same landscape block at the end. That block appears after shop styles. Put the shop rules inside it, after `.btn` rule. Then `.sheet-btn{height:42px}` wins if same specificity? `.btn` 0,1,0; `.sheet-btn` 0,1,0, later wins. Good.

Also the shop categories' min-height 78 might make 3 rows tighter; good.

Let's implement in the landscape block. Then rerun layout.

Also consider 844x390 orientation landscape but width>700 media query sets table size only. Fine.

