content.text:
Now chip CSS system. Replace lines 491-499 block with:
- universal mapper
- paid edge rule
- set variables
- preview generic later (we'll update preview block separately).

Let's craft exact CSS.

```
/* chip palettes: each set coordinates five denomination colors */
body[class*="chips-"] .chip-1{ --base:var(--c1,#e8e2d2); --label:var(--l1,#26333a); }
body[class*="chips-"] .chip-5{ --base:var(--c5,#bd3b32); --label:var(--l5,#fff7e6); }
body[class*="chips-"] .chip-25{ --base:var(--c25,#1c7a4e); --label:var(--l25,#fff7e6); }
body[class*="chips-"] .chip-100{ --base:var(--c100,#242525); --label:var(--l100,#ffe6a8); }
body[class*="chips-"] .chip-500{ --base:var(--c500,#6c3a86); --label:var(--l500,#fff7e6); }
body:not(.chips-classic) .chip{ --edge:var(--set-edge,#f1e6cf); }
body:not(.chips-classic) .chip span{ text-shadow:0 1px 1px rgba(0,0,0,.32); }
body:not(.chips-classic) .chip-1 span{ text-shadow:0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.22); }
```
Wait, the last sets light shadow for chip-1 labels; for dark labels a light shadow is better. Fine. For sets where chip-1 label is light (none? Midnight l1 maybe dark; all l1 dark), so light shadow is good. Classic excluded.

Set vars:
```
body.chips-sunset{--c1:#ffd166;--c5:#f4a259;--c25:#e76f51;--c100:#c44569;--c500:#7a2e52;--set-edge:#ffe3b0;--l1:#3a2110;--l5:#3a1f10;--l25:#3a1712;}
```
Check `--l25` dark on #e76f51: contrast likely good. `--l100`, `--l500` fallback white.
Ocean: `--c1:#8fe3cf;--c5:#35b8b0;--c25:#1b8a9c;--c100:#22638f;--c500:#243b6b;--set-edge:#c6f4ff;--l1:#123a38;--l5:#0d3332;`
Forest: `--c1:#c6dd85;--c5:#86b85e;--c25:#4f9451;--c100:#2b6b4a;--c500:#174436;--set-edge:#e0edb8;--l1:#253312;--l5:#1b2c12;`
Candy: `--c1:#ffb3d1;--c5:#ffc09b;--c25:#c9a7f5;--c100:#64c7a2;--c500:#b24b83;--set-edge:#fff0f6;--l1:#3b1a26;--l5:#3a2117;--l25:#2a1c3f;--l100:#0f332a;`
Royal: `--c1:#f0d58a;--c5:#bf95e8;--c25:#9a6ad8;--c100:#6f3fb0;--c500:#34245f;--set-edge:#f2e3b0;--l1:#3a2c10;--l5:#261741;` For l5 dark on #bf95e8 contrast maybe good. `--l25` fallback white okay on #9a6ad8 (contrast? #9a6ad8 vs white 4.0, okay).
Ruby: `--c1:#f4b1b1;--c5:#e4687a;--c25:#c53b55;--c100:#941f3e;--c500:#5b142b;--set-edge:#ffe0e0;--l1:#3a1414;` l5 white on #e4687a contrast ~3.0; maybe dark label for l5 (#3a1118) gives high contrast. Use l5 dark. l25 white on #c53b55 ~5.0. Good.
Gold: `--c1:#f4df9a;--c5:#e8bf62;--c25:#c9993e;--c100:#9a6c25;--c500:#5c4319;--set-edge:#fff2bf;--l1:#3a2c10;--l5:#392a10;--l25:#34240c;`
Midnight: `--c1:#9ab7e8;--c5:#5f83c4;--c25:#3c5a99;--c100:#263a68;--c500:#141f3d;--set-edge:#bfc9ff;--l1:#13213d;--l5:#0d1730;`
Neon: `--c1:#f9f871;--c5:#ff5da2;--c25:#52f7ff;--c100:#a6ff4d;--c500:#8a5cff;--set-edge:#ffffff;--l1:#28300c;--l5:#3b0f2b;--l25:#0b3336;--l100:#26330c;`
Check all 10 sets: classic + 9.

Preview generic:
```
.cosmetic-preview[class*="chips-"] i:nth-child(1){background:var(--c1,#c8372f);}
.cosmetic-preview[class*="chips-"] i:nth-child(2){background:var(--c25,#1c7a4e);}
.cosmetic-preview[class*="chips-"] i:nth-child(3){background:var(--c100,#242525);}
.cosmetic-preview[class*="chips-"] i{border-color:var(--set-edge,rgba(255,255,255,.72));}
```
But this generic selector includes `.cosmetic-preview.chips-classic` and the background vars? For classic no c vars, fallbacks red/green/black. Good. Specific classic rules can be removed. The third element edge for classic becomes white instead of gold; acceptable but maybe we can keep `.cosmetic-preview.chips-classic i:nth-child(3){border-color:#d8b45e}` after generic. Nice.

The preview `i` are on a span with class `chips-*`, but body also has one; set vars inherited. Good.

Edge `--set-edge` on preview: body set; yes.

One issue: `body[class*="chips-"] .chip-1` sets `--label` with fallback; but `.chip-1 span` color uses `color:var(--label)` inherited from chip? `.chip` sets `color:var(--label)`; yes. Good.

The chip set variables are on body and inherit into chip elements. The mapper reads them. Good.

Let's replace.

